<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jukun people</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jukun are a people of the middle Benue valley in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, living mainly in Taraba and neighbouring states. They are identified with the power called Kwararafa in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bornu">Bornu</a> sources, which raided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kano">Kano</a> and other Hausa cities in the 17th century. Their sacred king, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aku-uka">Aku Uka</a>, whose wellbeing was bound to the harvest, still reigns at Wukari.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the seventeenth century the Kwararafa (<b>Jukun</b>) confederacy from the Benue valley raided Kano and Katsina.</blockquote><a href="/empire/hausa-kingdoms">Hausa kingdoms · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>He began campaigning in 1804, among the first commanders to take the field, and built an emirate out of conquests over local peoples on the borders of the Kanem-Bornu Empire and the <b>Jukun</b> lands.</blockquote><a href="/state/gombe-emirate">Gombe Emirate</a></li><li><blockquote>Its traditions point to links with both the <b>Jukun</b> of Kwararafa and the Yoruba and Benin worlds, and the royal dynasty is associated with Ayegba om'Idoko, a celebrated early Attah.</blockquote><a href="/state/igala-kingdom">Igala Kingdom</a></li><li><blockquote>Wukari emerged as the main <b>Jukun</b> centre as the older Jukun power, Kwararafa, declined in the 18th century.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-wukari">Kingdom of Wukari</a></li><li><blockquote>Kwararafa is the name used in Hausa and Bornu sources for a power centred on the <b>Jukun people</b> of the middle Benue.</blockquote><a href="/state/kwararafa">Kwararafa</a></li><li><blockquote>He established a separate emirate, centred first on Muri, among the <b>Jukun</b>, Mumuye and other peoples, and it was later recognised directly by Sokoto.</blockquote><a href="/state/muri-emirate">Muri Emirate</a></li></ul></section>
